    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 3/3 tests, no failures). The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nTelephone numbers are now stored and returned in E.164 form, with duplicate detection comparing E.164 values. The change is confined to the `POST /api/owners` pipeline plus the entity constraint.\n\n**New \u2014 `Telephones.java`** (`rest/function/owner/`): a small utility with `toE164(String)` that:\n- strips spaces, dashes and brackets (`[\\s\\-()]`);\n- keeps a leading `+` and country code when present, otherwise assumes `+61` and drops a single leading `0` from the national digits;\n- requires 8\u201315 digits after the `+`, returning `null` when no valid E.164 can be formed.\n\nSo `\"0412 345 678\"` \u2192 `\"+61412345678\"` and `\"+64 21 123 456\"` \u2192 `\"+6421123456\"`.\n\n**`RequireOwnerFields.java`**: replaced the old \"strip to digits, require exactly 10\" normalization with `Telephones.toE164(...)`; a `null` result throws `RequiredFieldsException` \u2192 **400**.\n\n**`RequireUniqueTelephone.java`**: now compares E.164 values (`Telephones.toE164` of the request vs. each existing owner) instead of the old digits-only forms.\n\n**`model/Owner.java`**: the entity's telephone bean-validation was `@Digits(integer=10)` + `@Pattern(\"^[0-9]{10}$\")`, which rejected the `+`-prefixed value at persist time (the initial 500 I hit). Replaced with `@Pattern(\"^\\\\+[0-9]{8,15}$\")` (kept `@NotEmpty`, removed the now-unused `@Digits` import).\n\nThe three acceptance tests (`coreNationalToE164`, `functionalityKeepsExplicitCountryCode`, `errorRejectsUnformattable`) and the full suite are green.\n\nOne note: `openapi.yml` still declares the request/response DTO telephone `pattern: '^[0-9]*$'`, but it isn't enforced (the endpoint binds `@RequestBody` without `@Valid`, and response DTOs aren't validated), so it doesn't affect behaviour \u2014 I left it untouched. I can tighten that schema too if you'd like the generated contract to reflect E.164.",
